{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fd7701de3a3d42d7","name":"ARC-170 Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-fd7701de3a3d42d7","title":"ARC-170 Starfighter","revision":15611,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:53Z","sha256":"e3fdf25ebff79922e9c908e0809482aae01fcd7af718e172c440919e260f3bd5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15611","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=ARC-170%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fd7701de3a3d42d7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["These rugged and durable attack fighters can handle independent raids as well as assaults on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". Their powerful shields, robust armor, and tail ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," give them good odds even when surrounded by enemy fighters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Aggressive ReConnaissance fighter, or ARC-170- developed as a joint venture by the Incom and Subpro Corporations- serves as both a long-range scout and a heavy assault fighter. The ARC-170 is part of a line of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Z-95 Headhunter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Z-95_Headhunter","referenceId":"reference:c01adb1b99b911a6"},", that eventually led to the development of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:3633fb1b1140ece1"},". The narrow frame, flanked by powerful twin engines and S-foils, was innovative at the time of the ARC-170's introduction. Though it served with distinction during the latter days of the Clone Wars, the fighter was never built in the vast numbers of many other designs.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ARC-170's ultimate failing was not lack of firepower or ability, but the high supply cost to keep it in combat. The Starfighter needs regular maintenance and requires a three-person crew, making it expensive in terms of training, personnel, and upkeep. As a result, once the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"}," replaced it in Imperial squadrons, there was very little demand for the ARC-170. Though some were liberated by the Rebellion, most were mothballed or scrapped simply because the Rebels lacked the flight crews and repair bays necessary to keep the older ARC-170s ready for combat.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ARC-170 is a heavy-hitting fighter, with long-range capabilities and enough stowage to operate for 5 days without resupply. Though taxing, it was possible for the crew to sleep in shifts, allowing the Starfighter to be alert and ready for action for days at a time. This made it popular as a scout and a picket ship, keeping an eye on likely targets, enemy forces, or even friendly planets until larger ships could arrive for permanent duty. An ARC-170 could be sent deep into enemy territory, and its shields gave it a good chance of surviving even if it ran into a larger force of fighters when performing such missions. The durability and range of the vessel came at a cost, however. The ARC-170 has slow acceleration and poor maneuverability compared to smaller fighters.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["ARC-170 Starfighter Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28; +8 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 150; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 25; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 48\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 16 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.mirahe